WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:05.540
This is the world as Vincent van Gogh saw
it -- or, at least, how the makers of the

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.060
film "Loving Vincent" imagine he did.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.860
They've created this animated feature as a
homage to the Dutch artist.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:19.280
It's comprised of around 65-thousand frames
-- each painted in oil, by hand.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.640
The film had its world premiere in very picturesque
surroundings in southeastern France.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:33.320
"Loving Vincent" was shown as part of the renowned Annecy International Animation Film Festival.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:43.260
“When you put these paintings together and
put the letters together, they almost create

00:00:43.269 --> 00:00:45.460
like a storyboard.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:50.440
So that was the main reason.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:58.719
And also he fascinated me as an artist with
his incredible bravery and the passion that

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:02.020
still breathes life into what we’re doing.”

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.740
The film's storyline is based on around 800
letters that Vincent van Gogh wrote to his

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.780
brother Theo.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:14.530
It covers the last year of the artist's life,
including his struggles with mental illness

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:16.680
and his eventual suicide.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.370
“Then he comes here with a girl who, I reckon,
was out of his league, and the next thing

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:22.820
I hear he's killed himself.”

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:28.900
Around 100 of Van Gogh's paintings provided
the basis for the film's artwork.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:39.740
“A big challenge was for us to be unified
as the team of painters, because they are

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:47.500
very different people with their artistic
background and different styles.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:53.660
And all of a sudden, they all had to just
leave all of that behind.”

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.460
First, the scenes were filmed using actors.

00:01:57.469 --> 00:02:02.509
These images served as templates for the painters,
who recreated them frame by frame in van Gogh's

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:04.650
own signature style.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:09.080
"The truth is: I'm not important."

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.140
The artists worked at three different locations.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:17.239
Most painted their works in Gdansk, Poland.

00:02:17.239 --> 00:02:21.680
Some 5-thousand people from around the world
had applied to take part in the project.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.540
Around 100 made the grade.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.880
To make the artists' work easier,

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.040
these special studios were set up.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.060
Each one is equipped with a monitor and a
projector.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.860
When required, the template can be projected
onto the screen.

00:02:41.769 --> 00:02:46.100
Kateryna Ocheredko from Ukraine specializes
in portraits.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:49.010
Vincent van Gogh is one of her idols.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:54.319
"I use his experience for my work and for
my life.

00:02:54.319 --> 00:02:58.880
And now I can do something for him.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:07.480
I think, because he is very important and
he changes our thoughts on colors, about styles

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.350
and work in landscape.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:11.440
It’s my thank you for him."

00:03:11.849 --> 00:03:16.320
Every painting was photographed and pieced
together to create a film sequence.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:19.700
It took 12 paintings to produce just one second
of film.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:23.060
Their style had to remain as close as possible
to van Gogh's,

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:25.320
but at times they had to get creative.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:30.120
"Van Gogh painted various canvas sizes, so
sometimes we had to invent a little bit to

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.520
the right and to the left.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:37.080
Sometimes for script reasons we actually had
to change the season.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:40.980
So we had to change a little bit the color
scheme in some of the paintings a bit.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:47.280
But we tried to show most of the paintings
as true to the original at some point in the

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.709
film as we can."

00:03:48.709 --> 00:03:54.300
At the Animation Film Festival in Annecy,
the film seems to have found its audience.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:02.220
“That everything is animated and that they're
all paintings is just....I can hardly believe it.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.700
And the play of light and shadow, and that
everything is also painted in impressionist style..."

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:16.380
“You were really caught up in the paintings
of Vincent van Gogh.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.720
This film was very touching and poetic.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:22.200
You had the impression of being caught up
in the artist's emotional torment."

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.700
"Loving Vincent" is set to hit cinema screens
this fall.

